Engineering Proposal

DATE:				7.30.2024

SUBMITTED TO:		Arnaud Schwab- Ketiv Technologies 

PROJECT:			Old Castle BMC TC6 and TC12

SUBMITED BY:		Andy Johnston, P.E.

Johnston Engineering offers the following engineering services:

# Scope:

- Analysis of recently tested prototype TC6 hardware: (40-80 hours) 

- Material properties research

- Structural analysis 

- Tuning materials properties to represent previous test data 

- TC6 weight reduction studies: (40-80 hours)

- Structural analysis of customer provided models.  Target weight reduction of 25% over prototype hardware. 

- Generation of new CAD geometry for reduced weight design. 

- Iteration between new CAD geometry and structural analysis until target weigh achieved. 

- Design TC12 (40-80 hours)

- Use results from TC6 structural analysis to design a larger TC12 cover 3D CAD file 

- Structural analysis of newly generated CAD file

- Generate results report: (20 hours)

- Structural analysis results presentations documenting assumptions, material properties, comparison to tested configuration, results and recommendations. 

# Deliverables:

- Structural analysis results presentations documenting assumptions, material properties, comparison to tested configuration, results and recommendations.

- New TC12 3D CAD file in Solidworks, STEP or IGES format at customer discretion.  

# Exclusions:

# Cost: 

The project is offered on a time and materials hourly basis at $195/hour.   Analysis is estimated to require 140-180 hours engineering time ($27,300-$50,700)

